"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Akīka is a silica mineral (SiO2). It is the banded form of Chalcedony."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/gairika","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Red Ochre","la":"Gairika"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Gairika is Red Ochre, an oxide of Iron (Fe2O3). This mostly earthy \nvariety of hematite mineral is also known as Reddle."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/gandhaka","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Sulphur","la":"Gandhaka"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Gandhaka is sulphur (S), a non-metallic solid element."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/godanti","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Selenite / Gypsum","la":"Godantī"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Godantī is Selenite (CaSO4, 2H2O) mineral."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/gomeda","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Zircon / Hessonite","la":"Gomeda"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Gomeda is Almandite {Fe3Al2 (SiO4)3}, one of the garnet group of \nminerals."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/jaharamohara","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Serpentine","la":"Jaharamoharā"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Jaharamoharā is Serpentine, a hydrous silicate of Magnesium \n[Mg6(Si4O10)X(OH)8 ]. This is also known as Green Marble in \ntrade."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/kanta-lauha","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Loadstone / Magnetite","la":"Kānta Lauha"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Kānta Lauha is an Iron ore containing magnetite, a ferric oxide \n(Fe3O4) mineral."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/kasisa","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Ferrous Sulphate","la":"Kāśīśa"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Kāśīśa is Ferrous Sulphate (FeSO"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/khatika","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Kaolinite / Chalk","la":"Khaṭikā"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Kha°ikā is Kaolinite (Al2 (Si2O5) (OH) 4), an aggregate of minerals and \n colloidal substances commonly known as Clay."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/mandura","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Iron Slag","la":"Maṇḍūra"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Maṇ²ūra is a metallic oxide-cum-silicate of iron, generally \nhaving the composition Fe2SiO4 and commonly called Slag."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/rajata","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Silver","la":"Rajata"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Rajata (Ag) is a silver- white metal available in the form of ingots."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/samudra-lavana","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Sea Salt","la":"Sāmudra Lavaṇa"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Sāmudra Lavaṇa is a halite mineral, described as Sea salt (NaCl)."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/sankha","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Borax","la":"Śaṅkha"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"ṭa¬kaṇa is Borax mineral (Na2B4O7, 10 H2O), also known as Tincal."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/sauvira-anjana","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Antimony / Lead ore","la":"Sauvirāñjana"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Sauvīrāñjana is a lead ore containing galena (PbS) mineral."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/svarna-maksika-sandrita","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Copper Concentrate","la":"Svarṇamākṣika Sāndrita"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Svarṇamākṣika-Sāndrita \nis \na \ncopper \nconcentrate \ncontaining \nChalcopyrite (CuFeS2) mineral with minimum 12 % copper content. \n(Svarṇamākṣika-Sāndrita, herein after, is referred as Sāndrita \nSvarṇamākṣika in the rest of the monograph)."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/svarna-maksika","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Copper Pyrites","la":"Svarṇamākṣika"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Svarṇamākṣika is a copper ore containing Chalcopyrite (CuFeS2) \nmineral."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/svarna","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Gold","la":"Svarṇa"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Svarṇa (Au) is a yellow metal available in the form of ingots."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/tamra","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Copper","la":"Tāmra"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Tāmra is the end product of the metallurgical process of Copper ore. It \nis available in the form of wires, sheets or rods of Copper which is \nproduced by an electrolytic process."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/tuttha","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Copper Sulphate","la":"Tuttha"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Tuttha is copper sulphate (Cu SO4, 5H2O), also known as blue vitriol, \ncopper vitriol, blue stone or chalcanthite mineral."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/vaikranta","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Tourmaline","la":"Vaikrānta"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"metals","definition":{"en":"Vaikrānta is Tourmaline, sodium aluminium borosilicate of the \nformula [(Ca, Na)X(Mg, Al6)X{B3 Al2 Si6X(O,OH)30}]"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/1-1","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"la":"Nessler Cylinders"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"test-methods","definition":{"la":"Converted from ontology/data/test-methods/test-1-1.jsonld"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/1-2","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"la":"Sieves"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"test-methods","definition":{"la":"Converted from ontology/data/test-methods/test-1-2.jsonld"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/1-3","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"la":"Thermometers"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"test-methods","definition":{"la":"Converted from ontology/data/test-methods/test-1-3.jsonld"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/1-4","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"la":"UV Lamps"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"test-methods","definition":{"la":"Converted from ontology/data/test-methods/test-1-4.jsonld"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/1-5","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"la":"Volumetric Glassware"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"test-methods","definition":{"la":"Converted from ontology/data/test-methods/test-1-5.jsonld"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/1-6","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"la":"Weights and Balances"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"test-methods","definition":{"la":"Converted from ontology/data/test-methods/test-1-6.jsonld"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/1-7","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"la":"Muslin Cloth"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"test-methods","definition":{"la":"Converted from ontology/data/test-methods/test-1-7.jsonld"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ayp/monographs/2-2-1","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"la":"Net Content"},"edition":"API Part I–VII","category":"test-methods","definition":{"la":"Conv